<<!DOCTYPE type=`memetic-wikitext+tiddlywiki` spec=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/memetic-wikitext`>>

<<^ code=`&#x0001;` from=`?` to=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/afford/engine.meme.projects`>>
<<^ code=`&#x0002;`>>

```toml meta
cacheable = true
l-space   = "stable"
role      = "render a meme to a target: md, html, tid or json"
tags      = ["lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/affordance", "lar:///engine.meme.projects"]
title     = "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/afford/engine.meme.projects"
type      = "text/memetic-wikitext+tiddlywiki"
uri-path  = "ha.ka.ba/lares/afford/engine.meme.projects"
```

<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! engine.meme.projects ~ render a meme to a target

`uri` names the meme and `to` the target (md, the submission markdown; html; tid; json); the target rides as a param, never a suffix. The carrier text itself reads through `get title=<uri> aperture=arc`. Deterministic and clock-free: currency proves by re-projecting.

The address stands ''candidate'' until the operator reads the landing's list. The MCP seat runs this act in its own process: the vessel's `call` binds the params against this carrier's live `#/takes` and answers `handler/seat` with the bound params, and the seat runs them (`act(address="lar:///engine.meme.projects", args={…})`).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/takes`>>

!! takes ~ uri · to · recipe · bag · realm · target · out · dialect · tongue · check · root

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`arg` name=`uri` params=`takes/word needs/required seat/1 as/<source> ~ the meme: its lar: address, or on the terminal a carrier file`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`to` params=`takes/word needs/required ~ the target: md, html, tid or json`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`recipe` params=`takes/word ~ the wiki (default names the worn face's daemon wiki)`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`bag` params=`takes/word ~ one bag`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`realm` params=`takes/id skins/cli ~ beside bag, the realm whose registration resolves it`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`target` params=`takes/handle skins/cli ~ another lit face whose daemon wiki the read visits, by handle or pet name`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`out` params=`takes/host-path skins/cli ~ the md pair's directory, or the rendered file; stdout otherwise`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`dialect` params=`takes/word skins/cli ~ (to md) a standalone RFC 7764 variant, its frontmatter carried inside the pair`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`tongue` params=`takes/bcp47 skins/cli ~ (to md) the BCP 47 tongue the sigil head names weave in`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`check` params=`takes/host-path skins/cli ~ (to md) prove a pair's currency by re-projection over a file.md or a shelf; writes nothing, exits 1 on drift`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`root` params=`takes/host-path skins/cli ~ (with check) the tree a pair's source resolves from; else the checkout`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/gate`>>

!! gate ~ seat

Testimony: the door checks; this slot grants nothing.

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`gate` name=`seat` params=`who/seat-or-hand ~ the vessel verbs the seat's handler reaches check the face's cap and the asker's hand themselves; a hand act refuses a seat by its own code`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/skins`>>

!! skins ~ cli · mcp

<<~ ahu slot=`#/skins/cli`>>

!!! lares meme project

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`skin` name=`cli` params=`handler/host spells/[[lares meme project]] ~ the terminal; a file with --to md renders in-process, any other target or a lar: source rides the vessel`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/skins/mcp`>>

!!! act lar:///engine.meme.projects

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`skin` name=`mcp` params=`handler/seat spells/[[act lar:///engine.meme.projects]] ~ the seat runs it in its own process`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

